// The -1/-1 counter ([CR#122.1a]): each subtracts 1 from power and toughness
// in layer 7c ([CR#613.4c]), conferred directly as the ability-free `Property`
// flavor. That conferral is what ONE counter confers; the model applies it
// once per counter held, so it reads no count.
//
// The annihilation rule ([CR#704.5q,122.3]) is the second conferral, a
// state-based one, which applies once per holder per check and may read
// counts (ruling 2026-10-10): if the permanent has both a +1/+1 and a -1/-1
// counter, N of each are removed from it at once, where N is the smaller of
// the two counts. The two removals are one simultaneous action, as every
// state-based action of a check is one event ([CR#704.3]), not one pair per
// sweep. It lives here rather than on `p1p1Counter`, which points at it.
//
// The rule names this kind by its bare name inside its own definition: a
// declaration's name means its kind everywhere (ruling 2026-10-10).
CounterKind(
    name: "m1m1Counter",
    params: [],
    compound_stem: Measure,
    compound_onset: Consonant,
    spelling: "-1/-1",
    holder: Object,
    confers: [
        boost(down(1), down(1)),
        stateBased(
            matches(This, and([hasCounters(p1p1Counter), hasCounters(m1m1Counter)])),
            simultaneously([
                removeCounters(
                    exactlyOf(smallerOf(countersOn(p1p1Counter, This), countersOn(m1m1Counter, This))),
                    p1p1Counter,
                    This,
                ),
                removeCounters(
                    exactlyOf(smallerOf(countersOn(p1p1Counter, This), countersOn(m1m1Counter, This))),
                    m1m1Counter,
                    This,
                ),
            ]),
        ),
    ],
)
